From 526f91f076b496feab82ebaf9da6c1c80fad5c5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 12:47:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Bake product/gallery/settings data into static build to
 eliminate cold starts

The static site was already CDN-hosted and cold-start-proof, but products.js,
gallery.js and app.js called the live API (/api/products, /api/gallery,
/api/categories, /api/settings) on every page load to get product data,
prices and contact details. That API runs on Render's free plan, which sleeps
after 15 min idle, so browsing still incurred the full 10-30s cold start even
though Cloudinary had already made image loads themselves fast.

build-static.sh now fetches that data at build time and writes it into
dist/data/*.json, shipped alongside the static pages. A new fetchData()
helper in config.js reads that snapshot on the static site (falling back to
the live API for local dev or if a file is missing). Browsing is now fully
served from the CDN with no live backend dependency.

Quote submission, order tracking, admin login and all admin edits are
unchanged -- still live calls to the backend. Publishing content changes to
the static snapshot remains a deliberate action via the existing "Update
website now" button on the admin Website tab (publish.js, AUTO_PUBLISH stays
off by default); its copy now reflects that content changes need a publish
to reach visitors, not just layout changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0177efB2zKYqBKVDfJLKCQ5k
